1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,271
Shopping for something that has to fit? Meet Tesselle - a personal shopping agent built with Gemini and Google Cloud.

2
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:15,638
This is the live app. The guided demo runs itself - real agents, real web search, nothing pre-recorded.

3
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:24,471
This demo runs itself on the live app. Gemini agents do every step; real stores and real makers are searched as it happens.

4
00:00:25,367 --> 00:00:31,898
Start the way you like - words, voice, a photo or a video. Here: a sentence and a photo of the desk.

5
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:40,937
Gemini reads the words and the photo together, and writes a brief: what must stay the same, and what is just nice to have.

6
00:00:41,599 --> 00:00:51,370
Here is the brief. Every must-have - like the 18 centimetre depth - is kept unless you agree to change it. You can edit any of it, any time, on the right.

7
00:00:52,733 --> 00:01:00,744
The design agent draws a concept from the brief, so you can picture it. It is clearly labelled as an illustration, never an offer.

8
00:01:01,666 --> 00:01:12,197
Now the shopping agent and the maker scout search real stores and real makers that deliver to Chennai, using Google Search grounding. Every result links to its real page.

9
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:24,844
No ready-made matches confirm depth under 18 cm, but custom makers can build it. Each listing was checked against the brief by plain code - a pretty one that is too deep never gets through.

10
00:01:25,766 --> 00:01:32,217
If nothing ready-made fits, real makers can make it exactly. Tesselle writes the message for you.

11
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:40,784
The outreach agent wrote it - only your brief, never your name or address. You send it yourself, from your email or WhatsApp.

12
00:01:41,899 --> 00:01:49,790
When a maker replies, paste it or drop a screenshot. Here, a practice reply shows what happens when a seller pushes a change.

13
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:59,924
The workshop wants a 20 centimetre depth to suit its tools. Your shelf allows 18 - so the fit checker stopped it, and the choice is yours.

14
00:02:00,833 --> 00:02:08,724
Tesselle drafts your reply asking them to keep 18 centimetres. The practice workshop comes back with a layout that fits.

15
00:02:09,299 --> 00:02:15,790
One offer, one brief version, every must-have kept. Tesselle never pays or orders for you.

16
00:02:16,699 --> 00:02:21,350
You confirm the order with the maker, and mark it when it arrives - on any device.

17
00:02:22,266 --> 00:02:28,637
The delivery inspector compares a photo with the checks you agreed - and says honestly what a photo cannot prove.

18
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:35,497
From a sentence and a photo to a checked delivery, with every must-have kept. That's Tesselle.

19
00:02:36,599 --> 00:02:40,930
Tesselle. Imagine it. Keep what matters. Get it made.

